{
  "$Comment": "The Disenchanting Table block. It wears the vanilla Salvage bench's own model, textures and processing animation; the vanilla Bench and BlockEntity groups are left out because this block is a station, not a processing bench, and its Use runs RPG_Station_Disenchanting_Table_Use instead of the bench screen. The station engine flips the block between the states below: Default and Loaded are the resting looks (the Loaded look is the same model with a different hint), Working is the vanilla bench's processing look (the lit texture, the arms and door animation and the processing loop) with a green-gold light and the ember effect vanilla drew for this bench on its Fire part, and Drawing, which the ritual's Draw and Surge beats hold, is the same with a brighter light and denser tinted sparks. Every state name a station or a step names must exist here, or that flip silently does nothing. The Recipe makes the bare jar's table craftable at a tier 2 Workbench, where vanilla crafts its own Salvage bench: iron, wood, stone and a measure of Life essence. A pack that ships a same-id copy without a Recipe makes the table uncraftable and hands it out its own way.",
